To enact the protocol the flat would need to: (1) set a date within the next three days for a neutral meeting and agree on a brief agenda; (2) jointly select the chore‑board medium (paper poster, whiteboard, or a free app like Trello) and create the initial layout together; (3) write and circulate a one‑page communication contract that defines the pause‑and‑share step, the notification method for concerns, and the agreed consequence for repeated missed chores; (4) schedule a standing five‑minute slot each week (or an asynchronous update on the board) for schedule adjustments; (5) implement the weekly satisfaction rating on the board and collect the data; (6) after four weeks hold a review meeting to discuss the collected ratings and swap‑log, decide on any refinements (such as bringing in a neutral third‑party mediator if tensions persist), and commit to the next trial cycle.